From 423d773e79150a1acf0fc5eb98322a0c00379695 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 02:06:35 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(auxiliary): pool rotation names the failed wire model and
 credential [daveey]

_recover_provider_pool called mark_exhausted_and_rotate without model or
failure_reason, so the pool could not scope a generic Anthropic 429 to the
rate-limited model: every auxiliary 429 (goal judge, titles, compression)
benched the whole Claude credential for an hour although its quota windows
had room. The rotated retry's failure was reported with no credential at
all, so the pool benched whatever current() was.

- pass the failed request's wire model and a classified failure_reason
  (billing for payment/quota, rate_limit for 429) so billing/auth stay
  account-wide and a generic 429 benches only that model
- same-provider retries (sync and async) stamp the (api_key, model) they
  used on their exception; the ladder reports that identity for the
  rotated retry instead of none
---
 agent/auxiliary_client.py                     |  85 +++++--
 ...st_auxiliary_pool_model_scoped_rotation.py | 214 ++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 281 insertions(+), 18 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 tests/agent/test_auxiliary_pool_model_scoped_rotation.py

